        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: തടി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തടി (taṭi) — \"a trunk, timber\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inherited, and it does three jobs on one shape: the trunk of a standing tree, the sawn timber that comes out of it, and — of a person — bulk or build."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The third sense is ordinary Malayalam and not unkind. To say somebody has തടി (taṭi) is to say they are solidly made, and Kerala says it about a person the way English might say sturdy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Beside it sits തടിയൻ (taṭiyan), a heavy-set man, carrying that same he-word tail you met on the sun and the moon."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and this one describes people as well as trees."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
