        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: വിത്ത്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വിത്ത് (vittŭ) — \"a seed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inherited, matching Tamil vittu, and it closes the tree by going back to where the tree started."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Like വേര് (vērŭ) it travels into the abstract. The വിത്ത് (vittŭ) of a plan is its beginning, and Malayalam will talk about sowing one. The doubled tt in the middle is worth catching by ear — Malayalam holds it long, and the length is what separates this word from others in its neighbourhood."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sowing season in Kerala is set by the rains rather than by a date, which is why the farming words in this language lean on the weather more than on the calendar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run closes where a tree starts: a tree, a branch, the trunk, a root, a seed."
            }
          ]
        },
